%% One fx process refreshing a shared DPoP-bound Google Gemini login in Design A
%% (GeminiDpopRefresh.tla). Design A holds all seven safety invariants and Settles.
stateDiagram-v2
    state "Starting, reading saved login" as Starting
    state "Holding an access token" as Ready
    state "Waiting for the shared login lock" as WaitingLock
    state "Inside lock, checking saved login" as CheckingSaved
    state "Sending DPoP refresh request" as Refreshing
    state "Writing tokens and DPoP nonce atomically" as Saving
    state "Retrying API request with live token" as RetryingAPI
    state "Request succeeded" as Done
    state "Request failed, saved login kept" as Failed
    state "Saved login cleared, asking user to sign in" as NeedsSignIn

    [*] --> Starting
    Starting --> Ready : saved login found
    Starting --> NeedsSignIn : no saved login
    Ready --> Done : API accepts token
    Ready --> WaitingLock : 401 or under 300 s left
    WaitingLock --> CheckingSaved : lock acquired
    CheckingSaved --> NeedsSignIn : saved login gone
    CheckingSaved --> RetryingAPI : saved token is live, adopt and release lock
    CheckingSaved --> Refreshing : saved token is stale or rejected
    Refreshing --> Refreshing : 400 use_dpop_nonce on first try, update nonce
    Refreshing --> Failed : second use_dpop_nonce, or offline / 429 / 5xx
    Refreshing --> NeedsSignIn : 400 invalid_grant (grant expired or token spent), clear login
    Refreshing --> Saving : 200 OK with new tokens and rotated nonce
    Saving --> RetryingAPI : atomic write done, release lock
    RetryingAPI --> Done : API accepts token
    RetryingAPI --> Failed : second 401

%% Rule breaks in Design B and the mutants (check.sh shows each one fails):
%% design-b-no-rotate and design-b-rotate break SignOutSticks. Shortest path
%%   (7 steps): p1 reads token 0, refreshes at /token, and pauses before Save;
%%   SignOut deletes the saved login; p1's late Save restores it on disk.
%%   (design-b-rotate also breaks NoSpentRefresh at 10 steps when p1 and p2 race.)
%% mutant-signout-unlocked breaks SignOutSticks in the same 7-step trace.
%% mutant-decide-outside-lock breaks NoSpentRefresh. Shortest path (12 steps):
%%   p1 and p2 both read token 0 before locking; p1 locks, redeems 0 -> 1, and
%%   saves; p2 locks, decides from its stale pre-lock read 0, and sends spent 0.
%% mutant-unbounded-nonce-retry breaks NonceRetryAtMostOnce. Shortest path (9
%%   steps): server rotates nonce twice while p1 retries use_dpop_nonce 3 times.
%% mutant-clear-on-offline breaks ClearOnlyWithCause. Shortest path (6 steps):
%%   p1 hits an offline/429/5xx error and deletes the saved login.
%%
%% Events this chart leaves out:
%%   process killed at any step before settling (kernel drops any held lock;
%%     only a kill in Saving leaves a spent refresh token unpersisted),
%%   user sign-out (acquires lock in Design A and deletes the saved login),
%%   server nonce rotation, access token expiry, and 7-day grant expiry,
%%   Design B (no lock, in-memory nonce) and RotatesRefresh = FALSE.
